<title>FINLAND: NO RISK OF FINNISH CONSTRUCTION OVERHEATING - STTK.</title>
<headline>NO RISK OF FINNISH CONSTRUCTION OVERHEATING - STTK.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Talks of potential overheating in the Finnish construction sector are out of touch with reality, a senior official at the Confederation of Salaried Employees (STTK) said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>STTK department head Matti Hynynen also said a modest-pay-rise incomes settlement for 1998 onwards would only be possible if linked to &quot;fair&quot; tax decisions for wage earners.</p>
<p>He further called for an industrialisation programme along the lines proposed by three economics experts -- two new nuclear power plants, two new pulp mills and five new paper machines.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
